Fixes to the F# reader of lizard 1.26.1.

- A `member` of an object expression, `{ new I with member ... }`, is a
  function of its own.
- `let (|Even|Odd|) n`, `let (<+>) a b` and `static member (+)` are named by
  their symbols; `let (a, b) = ...` is a tuple pattern and names none.
- `member this.Item with get (i) = ...` reads `with get` as no parameters.
- Parameters are counted at the bracket depth of their own heading, also
  inside an object expression.

